# ui.artbloom — environment
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env*` is gitignored with `!.env.example`, so
# this file is the one that gets committed and it holds NAMES ONLY: never paste a
# key, a token or a URL with credentials in it here.
#
# NOTHING BELOW IS REQUIRED TO BUILD OR DEPLOY. With every value empty the site
# builds, renders and installs exactly as it does today: the catalogue is static,
# the CLI copies files, and error monitoring simply stays off. Fill these in when
# you want a deployment reporting errors to Sentry.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ IS A PROMISE, NOT A CONVENTION. Next inlines any variable with that
# prefix into the JavaScript sent to the browser, where it is readable by anyone who
# opens devtools. Everything without the prefix stays on the server. A Sentry DSN is
# safe to expose — it is a write-only ingest address, not a credential — but never
# move a real secret into that group.


# ─── site ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# PUBLIC. Absolute origin used for registry URLs, canonical links and OpenGraph
# tags — e.g. https://ui.artbloom.com. Read at build time by `lib/brand.ts`, which
# falls back to Vercel's own production URL and then to `origin` in `brand.json`,
# so a preview deploy is fine without it. No trailing slash.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=

# Set by Vercel, not by you: VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL is read as the fallback
# above. Listed here only so nobody wonders where it comes from.


# ─── sentry: error monitoring ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Create a project at sentry.io, then Settings → Client Keys (DSN). With
# no DSN set, `instrumentation.ts` and `instrumentation-client.ts` skip Sentry.init
# entirely — nothing loads, no events are sent, and the browser bundle is unchanged.

# PUBLIC. The browser DSN. Safe to expose, and it must carry the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
# to be readable on the client. Setting only this one enables monitoring everywhere,
# because the server reads it too when the server-only name below is empty.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=

# The server DSN. Optional: almost always the same value as the public one above.
# Kept as its own name so the server can report even if the public DSN is ever unset.
SENTRY_DSN=
